	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keyword: zj

Lists Zellij sessions (zellij list-sessions --no-formatting): current, running and EXITED (resurrectable). Subtitle shows state and age.

↩  attach in iTerm (zellij attach &lt;name&gt;; resurrects EXITED sessions)
   Typing a name that does not exist offers "New session '&lt;name&gt;'" (zellij attach -c &lt;name&gt;)
   With no sessions, ↩ starts an auto-named session
⌥↩ remove: kill-session for running sessions, delete-session for EXITED ones; result shown as a notification
⌘C copy session name

zellij path: /opt/homebrew/bin/zellij
Tests: /usr/bin/python3 -B -m unittest test_zj</string>
